  "assumptions": [
    "PostgreSQL is the target database; uuid primary keys are generated with gen_random_uuid() (pgcrypto/PG13+).",
    "A single role column on users (customer, courier, admin) is sufficient because each account has exactly one role; a roles/user_roles junction can be added if multi-role users are needed.",
    "Products represent both individual flowers and bouquets (product_type); bouquet composition is not modeled.",
    "Products can belong to multiple categories and have multiple colors, so product_categories and product_colors junction tables are used. Each junction table uses a surrogate id as its single primary key and a unique composite index on the FK pair.",
    "Orders are created only after successful payment; failed payment attempts are stored in payments with a null order_id, so no order exists for declined payments.",
    "Order delivery address and item prices/names are copied (snapshotted) into orders and order_items so history stays accurate when addresses or prices change.",
    "Card data is never stored; only Stripe identifiers and payment status are kept (PCI DSS handled by Stripe).",
    "Personal data (names, phones, addresses) is encrypted at rest at column or disk level, and a scheduled job purges data within 30 days of users.deletion_requested_at, anonymizing orders for financial records.",
    "Stock is decremented on order placement via application logic in a transaction; products.stock_quantity must remain >= 0 (CHECK constraint).",
    "Unique composite indexes are listed in the indexes arrays as 'col_a,col_b (unique)' since each table is limited to a single primary key column.",
    "Only the FK-owning side of each relationship is listed in relationships; inverse one-to-many relations are implied.",
    "Only users with role courier may be referenced by deliveries.courier_id and only role admin by deliveries.assigned_by; this is enforced in application logic.",
    "Order and delivery statuses are stored as varchar with allowed values enforced by CHECK constraints or application validation."
  ]
}